# Silver Traverse V1.3.1 — Exact Pink Pepper 10% — Blinded Validation Plan

**Formula:** `SILVER_TRAVERSE_V1_3_1_EXACT_PINK_PEPPER_10pct_30mL_20pct_THEORY.md`  
**Protocol ID:** ST-V1.3.1-EPP10-BLIND-20260828  
**Status:** THEORY PROTOCOL ONLY / NOT RUN / NO COMPOUNDING OR PROCUREMENT AUTHORIZED  
**Claim ceiling:** exact Pink Pepper identity, leadership, optimal dose, luxury, depth, completion, hedonism, liking, safety, stability, diffusion, longevity, and preference remain **NOT TESTED** or **HOLD** until separately authorized valid physical evidence exists

## Prerequisite HOLD Gate

Do not begin a physical block unless separately authorized and all applicable prerequisites are recorded:

- Pink Pepper bottle/container ID, exact label wording, user-bottle lot, oxidation state, and whether nominal 10% in DEP is w/w, w/v, or v/v; parent supplier/product is PerfumersWorld `Pink Pepper Essential Oil` `7SC00941`;
- applicable PW IFRA-document version and formula-category assessment, including the 2023 certificate/current-category-listing discrepancy;
- composite-natural identity/coverage decision; missing coverage remains HOLD and is not a modeled zero;
- Ambrox basis decision and future Peppermint working-stock record;
- all direct raw-stock aliquots at least 10 uL;
- immutable randomization sheet, blinded codes, container IDs, timestamps, and formula/source hashes;
- no skin testing unless separately authorized after safety review.

DEP carrier is established and supports constant-volume carrier controls. Unknown concentration basis blocks exact active-mass ppm, not raw-stock-volume dose response. Ownership and the theory formula remain valid at their stated ceiling.

## Decision Order

1. establish whether the owned exact material creates a recognizable integrated Pink Pepper object against a carrier-matched null;
2. locate a plausible dose within 240-480 uL of nominal 10% stock without using intensity as identity;
3. compare the selected exact-EO candidate with immutable V1.3 proxy control;
4. isolate whether 100 uL neat Helional protects or displaces Pink Pepper leadership against 80 and 60 uL constant-total arms;
5. test main-note leadership, temporal recurrence, spatial planes, pressure/release, comfort, and takeover separately;
6. only then reopen inherited musk, finishing, compression, and hedonic decisions.

## Common Evaluation Conditions

- Use two independent randomized blinded blocks on separate days.
- Assess blotter first at 0, 5, 30, and 120 minutes, then 6 and 24 hours.
- Evaluate first object and free description before any score.
- Keep identity, liking, intensity, depth, diffusion, comfort, and complexity as separate endpoints.
- Record anosmia/adaptation, environmental conditions, deviations, and confidence.
- A single preferred sample or a modeled OAV cannot establish the dose or identity.

## Stage 0 — Carrier-Matched Exact-Material Recognition

Remove the 480 uL identity module from the V1.3.1 formula to create a 5,520 uL common background. The background retains Benzyl Benzoate 60 uL and Geraniol 10% 30 uL. Use DEP as the constant-volume control carrier.

| Arm | 480 uL module | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| E480 | Pink Pepper EO 10% in DEP stock 480 | exact-material candidate: 48 uL nominal source-product equivalent / 8,000 nominal ppm |
| C480 | DEP 480 | carrier-matched no-Pink-Pepper control |

The exact material passes recognition only if both independent blocks freely recover a rosy-effervescent berry-bright woody pepper object in E480, with no matching recovery in C480 and no repeated carrier haze, hot/dry pepper, literal rose/plum, harshness, or fatigue. This supports recognition within the tested contrast, not universal identity or safety.

The contrast remains subject to stock-basis, lot, safety, and physical-authorization gates. DEP matching resolves the carrier identity only.

## Stage 1 — Carrier-Matched Dose Ladder

Use the same 5,520 uL common background and a fixed 480 uL identity module:

| Arm | Pink Pepper EO 10% in DEP stock | Added DEP | Nominal source-product ppm | Total module |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P240 | 240 | 240 | 4,000 | 480 |
| P360 | 360 | 120 | 6,000 | 480 |
| P480 | 480 | 0 | 8,000 | 480 |

All doses and compensators exceed the 10 uL floor. Choose no point merely because it is strongest. A dose survives only if it improves first-object Pink Pepper classification and recurrence while preserving cold/warm states, breathing middle, base identity, comfort, and re-smell desire without more fatigue or takeover. If P480 still fails leadership, the result is `NO WINNER IN TESTED RANGE`, not authority to jump to the 4,800 uL stock mapping of the historical ideal.

## Stage 2 — Exact EO versus Historical Proxy Candidate

Compare complete coded formulas:

- `E`: V1.3.1 exact-Pink-Pepper formula, 34 rows / 6,000 uL.
- `R`: immutable V1.3 reconstruction formula, 36 rows / 6,000 uL.

This whole-formula comparison is intentionally a candidate decision, not a chemical-equivalence experiment. It differs in exact Pink Pepper stock, proxy materials, Benzyl Benzoate, active fraction, and carrier load. E survives only if it repeatedly improves the named Pink Pepper object and integration while preserving or improving Silver Traverse fit, temporal recurrence, pressure/release, and liking without more harshness, fatigue, muddiness, carrier artifacts, or architectural collapse. R cannot be called equivalent if it wins.

## Stage 2B — Helional Leadership-Protection Ladder

Remove the current 100 uL neat Helional row from the selected exact-Pink-Pepper candidate to create a 5,900 uL common background. Restore a fixed 100 uL module in each arm; DEP is the constant-volume compensator and is not assumed olfactorily inert beyond this tested contrast.

| Arm | Helional neat | Added DEP | Nominal volume-derived concentrate mapping | Nominal finished-volume context at 20% | Hypothesis |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| H60 | 60 uL | 40 uL | 10,000 ppm-equivalent | 0.200% v/v | enough wet-mineral depth with maximum Pink Pepper headroom |
| H80 | 80 uL | 20 uL | 13,333 ppm-equivalent | 0.267% v/v | V1.2 bridge: fuller release without the H100 green/muguet risk |
| H100 | 100 uL | 0 uL | 16,667 ppm-equivalent | 0.333% v/v | current upper reference: deepest wet middle and highest takeover risk |

All direct aliquots are at least 20 uL. The ppm-equivalent figures are volume-normalized screening mappings, not authoritative ppm w/w; exact ppm w/w remains HOLD until an authorized mass ledger exists. Current local pipeline physics classifies H100 Helional as moderate at modeled opening OAV 28.8, but Pink Pepper is not validly modeled and neither value establishes sensory hierarchy.

Evaluate first-object identity at 0-5 minutes, then green/muguet/apple-blossom takeover, mineral depth, cloth continuity, pressure/release, Pink Pepper recurrence, comfort, liking, and fatigue at 30 minutes, 2 hours, 6 hours, and 24 hours. Do not select the lowest or highest dose by rule. Retain H100 only if it repeatedly improves wet-mineral depth or release over H80/H60 while Pink Pepper remains the freely named lead and no diffuse aquatic/muguet sport accord becomes the composition's identity. Prefer H80 or H60 if it preserves the same architecture with clearer Pink Pepper leadership. If H60 hollows the middle and H80/H100 both displace the subject, record `NO WINNER IN TESTED RANGE` rather than inventing an unblinded compromise.

## Stage 3 — Leadership and Temporal Recurrence

For the selected exact-EO and Helional doses, predeclare these checkpoints:

| Time | Required observation | Veto |
|---|---|---|
| 0-5 m | Pink Pepper is the first freely named object; citrus/mineral points frame it | lavender, citrus, mint, metallic ozone, or generic sport accord leads |
| 30-120 m | rosy-woody pepper remains classifiable through aromatic cloth and moving middle | literal rose/plum, hot Black Pepper, diffuse Hedione/muguet, fragmentation |
| 6 h | opening subject is recalled as peppered textile/root grain | generic ambrox/Iso E, lavender, musk, patchouli, or vetiver becomes the sole identity |
| 24 h | residue retains a recognizable subject echo without harsh woody pressure | blank musk/amberwood, sweet coumarin, resin takeover, or no recurrence |

Leadership requires repeated free-description and rank evidence. The formula name or material list cannot supply the answer.

## Stage 4 — One-Musk Tournament

Only after exact Pink Pepper and Helional doses survive Stages 0-3, compare constant-total 250 uL arms on the selected background:

| Arm | Musk module | Intended axis |
|---|---|---|
| H250 | Habanolide 250 | inward warm-skin comfort |
| R250 | Romandolide 250 | outward clean woody diffusion |
| E250 | Ethylene Brassylate 250 | creamy depth; lactonic takeover risk |
| N250 | Benzyl Benzoate 250 | no-musk control |

Use zero or one exact musk only. Select on Pink Pepper preservation, comfort, spatial fit, recurrence, liking, and fatigue—not on modeled projection or the existence of inventory.

## Stage 5 — Compression and Controlled Add-Backs

Apply the inherited V1.3 compression burden to the selected exact-EO/musk branch. Hide material count from evaluators. Prefer the compressed arm if it equals or improves named identity, states, planes, recurrence, transition, base identity, liking, and takeover profile. A removed row returns only after an isolated constant-total add-back produces its predicted localized effect in both independent blocks.

